\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RUttNP
< m1: T1
>

< m : UTT{UTTrec1}[head/T2]
>

   PARAMETERS
      <
       casespar : caseSETtype
      >

<
   SUBRULE
      < T1: NP{NPrec1}[mu1] >
      < T2: NP{NPrec2}[mu2] >

      COMP
         <
          C1: NPrec1.generic = nogeneric AND
              NPrec1.cases = [] AND
              QUOTE_polarityOK(T1) AND  
              (NOT QUOTE_varsintree(T1)) AND
              ( casespar = [nominative] OR
                casespar = [accusative] )
          A1: NPrec2.generic := omegageneric;
              QUOTE_AssignCase(NPrec1, mu1, NPrec2, mu2, casespar);
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: NPrec2.generic = omegageneric AND
              QUOTE_polarityOK(T2)
            C11: nominative IN NPrec2.cases
            A11: casespar := [nominative]
            C12: NPrec2.cases = [accusative]
            A12: casespar := [accusative]
          A1: QUOTE_AssignCase(NPrec2, mu2, NPrec1, mu1, []);
              NPrec1.generic := nogeneric;
              NPrec1.superdeixis := presentdeixis
         >
>
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RUttNP
\item[* relevant examples:]
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] UTTERANCE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class)
\item[* date of creation:] 08-JUN-1988 
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch RuttNp
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 07/07/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
added parameter to pass on case. If the case might be nominative, this is the 
only case that is accepted in analysis.
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To turn NPs into UTTs to be able to test and translate bare NPs.
Also, a check on polarity is performed.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) The model needs
a subrule to allow for the definition of a T1/T2, which is needed as input 
to the polarity checking function.
